SUMMARY:NBB 35th Anniversary Party ft. Virtuous + Natalie Brooke
DESCRIPTION:New Belgium Brewing is throwing it back to where it all began with a 35th Anniversary celebration inspired by the decade that made us. Join us for a nostalgic\, high-energy day as we party like it’s 1991! We will be honoring 35 years of community\, creativity\, and brewing fun.\nThe celebration takes place on Saturday\, June 27\, from 12 PM to 6 PM\, featuring a full lineup of entertainment\, local vendors\, a throwback giveaway\, activities\, and a community-centered atmosphere. Guests can expect a vibrant mix of experiences designed for all ages.\nLive music will set the tone throughout the day\, with performances from Virtuous 1 pm to 3 pm and Natalie Brooke 5 pm to 7 pm\, bringing the spirit of the 90s to life on stage.\nEvent highlights include:\n– Local vendors showcasing unique goods and services– Activities\, giveaways\, and games– A festive 90’s costume contest (so break out your best throwback looks!\nThis milestone celebration is more than just a party\, it’s an ode to the culture\, creativity\, and community that shaped New Belgium Brewing over the past 35 years.\nCome celebrate with us and raise a glass! Cheers to 35 years!
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/nbb-35th-anniversary-party/
LOCATION:New Belgium Brewing
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:LiveMusicAsheville.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T210000
DTSTAMP:20260624T190857Z
CREATED:20260624T190520Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260624T190857Z
UID:10071369-1782567000-1782594000@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:Jazz Foundation of America presents: A Great Day in Marshall
DESCRIPTION:Keeping the Music Alive in Western North Carolina \nFollowing the devastation of Hurricane Helene\, Jazz Foundation of America (JFA) immediately stepped in to support the resilient music community of Western North Carolina. Through one-time emergency grants and new employment opportunities\, JFA has provided critical financial assistance to local musicians who suffered catastrophic losses of property\, instruments\, and income. Even now in 2026\, the region is still actively recovering from the storm’s long-term impacts\, which is why JFA chose this community for its continued support. \nOn June 27th\, JFA proudly returns to Marshall\, NC\, to present a special mini-festival called “A Great Day in Marshall.” The event’s name pays homage to “A Great Day in Harlem\,” the nickname of Art Kane’s historic photo “Harlem 1958” featuring 57 jazz legends. This iconic imagery serves as the inspiration for JFA’s historic\, long-running New York City gala that raises vital resources for the Jazz Foundation’s Musicians’ Emergency Fund. Bringing this spirit of community and resilience to North Carolina\, this free-admission festival will span six local venues\, directly creating 80 much-needed employment opportunities for deserving area musicians. This event celebrates the region’s enduring spirit and honors JFA’s ongoing commitment to helping vulnerable artists in need—one musician at a time. \nhttps://jazzfoundation.org/marshall/
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/jazz-foundation-of-america-presents-a-great-day-in-marshall/
LOCATION:Downtown Marshall
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music,Madison County
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/728213217_10162648716585653_7259913088029149589_n-e1782327912154.jpg
END:VEVENT
